# The machines the portal deploys daemons to over ssh, as fff-machine-ssh writes them into the portal account's
# ~/.ssh/config (the alias, its host and user) and ~/.ssh/known_hosts (the host key, pinned: never accepted on first use).
# One line each: alias, host (its tailnet MagicDNS name), ssh user, ed25519 host key. The alias is the machine's
# ssh_host in the portal (add_machine); "rydin@beast" finds the alias beast.
#
# Each key was checked on two paths (w537, 2026-10-06, measured from BEAST): m3, m5 and loth2800 against the key BEAST
# had trusted for weeks of deploys, beast against its own sshd over loopback, each equal to a fresh ssh-keyscan over the
# tailnet. A machine reinstalled (a new host key) or a new machine: put its key here (ssh-keyscan -t ed25519 <host>,
# checked on the machine itself with ssh-keygen -l -f /etc/ssh/ssh_host_ed25519_key.pub), then fffctl update, or
# deploy/vm/host/machine-ssh.sh --fix on the host.
#
# alias    host      user       ed25519 host key                                                     fingerprint
m3         m3        benryding  AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIJPzhFYZX4GtbGkBP2Fl8RqwkZaXjQ9fUWN9P+p+/OX3  # SHA256:dNKSZKv7qWFocpDj+Fe2B2XbsPgdqDdbZ7m1dtk6H9c
m5         m5        benryding  AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIBayZWjCWfjUsoRkWYw2VNcYjTdMXLXCNZeS7eETg+g5  # SHA256:Ss8og0lE5Gja7ZaGwAwDZw18DV3kUbsrIzU5ISOzWN4
Loth2800   Loth2800  Lothsahn   AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIETlsnzQENULciyaMBvln+JfwZ/G3lUR/66yugqBGq+b  # SHA256:pyzyAdXNTzuW3t2hUWl2/diAjCOyk95iClIBdGSOdkA
beast      beast     rydin      AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGgE0GjCLsOOdLNBCR5KKXguNoZCX0Mh7C3tZbQzCDQx  # SHA256:fc+q1NmEuZnNbsqKKVUh33w8Khh8tkTe6yo5laRKb0k
